IMPORT prelude

-- Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Bishop of Singapore" is (s 2(1)), what the Ordinance
-- empowers it to do (s 2(2), (3)), which old property it took over (s 3), how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 4), what a
-- Gazette notification proves (s 5), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSO1911.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 6. The Ordinance is dated 3 November 1911.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0227 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Ordinance is six sections long, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside
-- the Church it matters in two places: buying, leasing or taking a mortgage from the Corporation (s 2(3), s 4), and title to land that
-- was conveyed to "The Bishop of Singapore" before 1911 (s 3).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 4(1) refers (whether a
-- power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); what "the respective estates and interests" in s 3 are;
-- the Corporation's internal governance, about which the Ordinance says nothing.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 5 -- who is the Corporation, and what the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): Bishop Ferguson-Davie "and his successors in office who are Bishops of the Church of England and recognised by the Archbishop
-- of Canterbury for the time being as duly authorised to exercise the office of Bishop in the Settlements of Singapore, Penang and
-- Malacca shall be a body corporate, hereinafter called the Corporation", named "The Bishop of Singapore", with perpetual succession and
-- a corporate seal.
-- s 5: "A notification in the Gazette of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Bishop of Singapore shall be
-- conclusive evidence that such person was duly authorised to exercise the said office."
--
-- The two tests are both in the text and both are encoded as written. The 2020 Revised Edition still names the Church of England, the
-- Archbishop of Canterbury and the Settlements of Penang and Malacca. The Gazette proves authorisation only; on the words of s 5 it does
-- not prove that the person is a Bishop of the Church of England (an inference from the wording, not stated).
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is a Bishop of the Church of England` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is recognised by the Archbishop of Canterbury as authorised for the Settlements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds the office that is the Corporation` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is a Bishop of the Church of England`
    AND `the claimant`'s `is recognised by the Archbishop of Canterbury as authorised for the Settlements`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
    `the claimant`'s `appointment is notified in the Gazette`

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): the seal "may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew, as to the Corporation seems fit".
-- s 2(3): the Corporation "may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description and may sell,
-- convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable or immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit and may sue and be sued in respect of such property
-- in all Courts of Justice."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". The capacity to sue and be sued is given "in respect of such
-- property"; the Ordinance grants no other power (whether the general law supplies one is outside the text and not encoded).
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `be sued in respect of its property`
    `sue on a matter not about its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `sue in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `be sued in respect of its property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- property held before 1911 in the name of the Bishop`

-- s 3: "All immovable property situated in the Settlements of Singapore, Penang and Malacca heretofore conveyed or assigned to or vested
-- in 'The Bishop of Singapore', whether with or without the name of the ecclesiastic for the time being holding the office, is hereby
-- vested in the Corporation for the respective estates and interests for which the same is held."
--
-- "Heretofore" is read as before the Ordinance (3 November 1911): an inference from the word, not a date the section states. Movable
-- property is not swept in by s 3. Whether the deed named the individual bishop makes no difference.
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `Singapore`
    `Penang`
    `Malacca`
    `elsewhere`

DECLARE Holding HAS
    `is immovable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is situated in` IS A Place
    `was conveyed, assigned or vested in The Bishop of Singapore before the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deed names the individual bishop` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the place` IS A Place
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is in the Settlements` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `elsewhere` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 vests it in the Corporation` IF
        `the holding`'s `is immovable`
    AND `is in the Settlements` (`the holding`'s `is situated in`)
    AND `the holding`'s `was conveyed, assigned or vested in The Bishop of Singapore before the Ordinance`

§§ `4 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 4(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the Bishop of Singapore for the time being or his attorney duly authorised by a power of attorney
-- deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 and shall also be signed by the said Bishop for the time
-- being or his attorney so authorised as aforesaid."
-- s 4(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed and that the same
-- is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- Three things must all be true: the seal, its affixing in the presence of the Bishop or a deposited attorney, and the signature of the
-- Bishop or a deposited attorney. An attorney whose power was never deposited does not qualify. The witness and the signer need not be
-- the same person on the words of s 4(1) (each limb says "the Bishop ... or his attorney"); that reading is encoded.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Bishop for the time being`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a church officer with no power of attorney`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Bishop or a deposited attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Bishop for the time being` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 4 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Bishop or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the Bishop or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Bishop or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `6 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government or of any bodies politic or corporate or of any other persons
-- except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
